@startuml
title CrisisSync - Process 1: Resource Package Reservation, Task Completion, and Resource Release

|Dispatcher|
start
:Select task on live Event Status Screen\nand initiate resource reservation;

|TaskManagementController|
:Validate authenticated/authorized Dispatcher session (REQ-19);\nverify task state and TLS 1.3 transport (REQ-20);

if (Authorized Dispatcher\nAND task is Ready?) then ([no])
  |Dispatcher|
  :View refusal message\n(reservation not allowed);
  stop
else ([yes])
  |ResourceAllocationController|
  :Retrieve package (exactly 1 Field Commander)\nand available resources;

  |Dispatcher|
  if (Choose reservation mode) then ([Manual Reservation])
    :Select required available resources\n(<= 3 clicks, REQ-13)\nand confirm reservation;
  else ([Automatic Allocation])
    :Select allocation criterion\n(e.g., geographic proximity, REQ-04, REQ-05);
    |ResourceAllocationController|
    :Initialize alternative attempt count\nfor each package item to 0;
    note right
      REQ-15: Complete automatic allocation,
      including alternatives, within 3 seconds
    end note
    :Select the best available resource\nfor each package item;
    if (Available resource found\nfor every package item?) then ([no])
      |Dispatcher|
      :Receive automatic allocation failure alert\n(task remains Ready);
      stop
    else ([yes])
    endif
  endif

  |ResourceAllocationController|
  repeat
    :Begin one SQL transaction;\nlock and verify all selected resources;

    if (All locked resources Available?) then ([yes])
      :Mark every package resource Reserved;\ntransition task Ready to Active;\ncommit and respond within 1.5 s (REQ-01, REQ-14, REQ-18);
    else ([no (conflict)])
      :Rollback transaction;\nreserve no resources (REQ-02);
      if (Automatic Allocation?) then ([yes])
        if (Conflicting resource has\nalternative attempt remaining?\n(max 2 alternatives per resource)) then ([yes])
          :Increment that resource's attempt count;
          :Select next-best available alternative\nfor the conflicting resource (REQ-06, REQ-07);
          if (Alternative resource found?) then ([yes])
            :Substitute the conflicting resource;
          else ([no])
            |Dispatcher|
            :Receive allocation failure alert\nand view refreshed screen\n(task remains Ready, REQ-03, REQ-08);
            stop
          endif
        else ([no])
          |Dispatcher|
          :Receive allocation failure alert\nand view refreshed screen\n(task remains Ready, REQ-03, REQ-08);
          stop
        endif
      else ([no (manual)])
        |Dispatcher|
        :Receive conflict notification\nand view refreshed screen\n(task remains Ready, REQ-03);
        if (Select alternative resources\nand retry manually?) then ([yes])
          :Select available replacement(s)\nand confirm reservation;
        else ([no])
          stop
        endif
      endif
    endif
    |ResourceAllocationController|
  repeat while (Reservation committed?) is ([no (retry)]) not ([yes])

  fork
    |TaskManagementController|
    :Record reservation and Active transition\nin Audit Log (REQ-01);
  fork again
    |NotificationController|
    :Push task and resource statuses\nto relevant screens;
  end fork

  |Field Commander|
  :View assigned Active task on Event Status Screen\nand execute task in the field;
  :Report task completion;

  |TaskManagementController|
  :Validate session and assigned Field Commander (REQ-09, REQ-19);\nconfirm task is Active;

  if (Authorized Field Commander\nAND task is Active?) then ([no])
    |Field Commander|
    :View rejection message\n(task remains Active);
    stop
  else ([yes])
    |TaskManagementController|
    :Begin one SQL transaction;
    :Transition task Active to Completed;\nrecord completion timestamp (REQ-10);
    :Detach package resources;\nreturn non-faulty resources to Available\n(Faulty/In repair stays unchanged, REQ-11);
    :Set dependent tasks to Ready\nonly when every prerequisite is Completed (REQ-12);
    :Commit completion and release transaction;

    fork
      |TaskManagementController|
      :Record completion and resource\nrelease events in Audit Log;
    fork again
      |NotificationController|
      :Push Completed/Ready tasks and\nAvailable resources within 500 ms (REQ-17);
    end fork

    |Dispatcher|
    :View updated Event Status Screen;
    stop
  endif
endif

@enduml